      "text": "3 January: Circuito Chico and Victoria Island"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:25152ad0c634f823",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "e43e701405e9fd074583d00d9fc6adcd964fce760ea07e20ab18ded6352a824a",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-tsvc722k5p",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, set out on the Circuito Chico, or Small Circuit. This drive around Bariloche covers about 65 km and takes approximately four hours.\n\nFrom Playa Bonita you can see Huemul Island. From the top of Cerro Campanario, you can look out over the lakes and El Trébol lagoon.\n\nNext, take a catamaran across Lake Nahuel Huapi to Victoria Island. You may spot pheasants and peacocks around the lagoons. The island is home to a variety of plants and animals, and one of the main stops is a myrtle grove covering about 12 hectares.\n\nOptional rafting near the border costs 200 USD per person. A treetop canopy tour is also available for 130 USD per person."
    },
